WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.310 --> 00:00:02.570
- Thank you so much for being vulnerable

00:00:02.570 --> 00:00:04.250
and sharing your story.

00:00:04.250 --> 00:00:06.690
Being able to experience
it through your eyes

00:00:06.690 --> 00:00:09.910
was mind-blowing, extremely heartbreaking.

00:00:09.910 --> 00:00:11.860
So thank you.

00:00:11.860 --> 00:00:15.150
What's happened in your lives since

00:00:15.150 --> 00:00:18.574
participating in this documentary series?

00:00:18.574 --> 00:00:21.280
- Well, for my brother and
I, at this moment in time

00:00:21.280 --> 00:00:23.440
we don't really feel safe in this country.

00:00:23.440 --> 00:00:24.640
We don't feel welcome

00:00:24.640 --> 00:00:27.710
and it does seem like time
is running out for us.

00:00:27.710 --> 00:00:31.650
- Our appointment with ICE
was postponed indefinitely.

00:00:31.650 --> 00:00:33.270
So we were just in this limbo.

00:00:33.270 --> 00:00:34.900
We didn't know what was going on.

00:00:34.900 --> 00:00:36.180
- My father was detained

00:00:36.180 --> 00:00:38.810
and a week later he was
deported to Colombia.

00:00:38.810 --> 00:00:40.690
- I didn't even get to say bye to him.

00:00:40.690 --> 00:00:42.740
He just left for work like normally

00:00:42.740 --> 00:00:46.010
and I got a call saying they got him.

00:00:46.010 --> 00:00:50.100
At that point, I think everything changed.

00:00:50.100 --> 00:00:53.180
'Cause I never imagined in a million years

00:00:53.180 --> 00:00:55.150
that they would actually detain him.

00:00:55.150 --> 00:00:58.810
That this was something that
they were only going to do

00:00:58.810 --> 00:01:02.820
to people who committed crimes,
to murderers, to whatever.

00:01:02.820 --> 00:01:04.220
We're not safe in our house anymore.

00:01:04.220 --> 00:01:05.990
I haven't been in my house in a month.

00:01:05.990 --> 00:01:08.350
I haven't slept in my bed.

00:01:08.350 --> 00:01:10.020
It doesn't make any sense.

00:01:10.020 --> 00:01:13.580
My dad went through hell for eight days

00:01:13.580 --> 00:01:15.030
in these detainment centers.

00:01:15.030 --> 00:01:17.210
I think everybody at this point

00:01:17.210 --> 00:01:18.580
has an idea of what's going on.

00:01:18.580 --> 00:01:22.650
They have people locked up
in these cages, essentially.

00:01:22.650 --> 00:01:26.010
They sleep on the floors
with these aluminum blankets.

00:01:26.010 --> 00:01:29.920
In these rooms, they have
the lights on 24 hours a day.

00:01:29.920 --> 00:01:30.840
Being able to speak with him

00:01:30.840 --> 00:01:32.580
after the eight days that he was there,

00:01:32.580 --> 00:01:35.740
I'd never heard the pain
that he had in his voice

00:01:35.740 --> 00:01:36.853
ever in my life.

00:01:37.700 --> 00:01:40.800
I think he will be damaged
by that experience,

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:44.140
just being there for eight
days, for the rest of his life.

00:01:44.140 --> 00:01:45.340
It was an absolute hell.

00:01:47.180 --> 00:01:51.010
They're telling us that
they're going after us

00:01:51.010 --> 00:01:54.533
and that we could possibly
be in this same situation.

00:01:55.930 --> 00:01:59.243
This country's not livable for us anymore.

00:02:01.710 --> 00:02:03.220
- Hearing all these things really

00:02:03.220 --> 00:02:06.040
ruins your determination to stay.

00:02:06.040 --> 00:02:09.730
It really just makes you
think that could be me.

00:02:09.730 --> 00:02:10.810
That could be my parents.

00:02:10.810 --> 00:02:12.810
That could be my siblings.

00:02:12.810 --> 00:02:14.460
You don't want that.

00:02:14.460 --> 00:02:16.810
What's the point in pushing so hard

00:02:16.810 --> 00:02:20.723
if all you're gonna get is that?

00:02:23.080 --> 00:02:25.810
- What do you guys think
that you would be doing

00:02:26.890 --> 00:02:30.420
if you didn't have to worry about this?

00:02:30.420 --> 00:02:32.420
- I think about this every day.

00:02:32.420 --> 00:02:36.090
If this wasn't happening,
I'd be going through school.

00:02:36.090 --> 00:02:38.210
Just working hard to achieve
what I wanna achieve,

00:02:38.210 --> 00:02:40.260
which is being a civil engineer.

00:02:40.260 --> 00:02:42.250
I'd be living a normal life.

00:02:42.250 --> 00:02:46.113
I'd be living the life that
my next door neighbor does.

00:02:47.370 --> 00:02:49.913
It's nothing crazy, but
it's what I dream of.

00:02:51.158 --> 00:02:52.230
- Right.

00:02:52.230 --> 00:02:54.480
- We've never been able to travel anywhere

00:02:54.480 --> 00:02:55.313
outside of the country

00:02:55.313 --> 00:02:57.730
because ICE has our passports

00:02:57.730 --> 00:02:59.610
and the only way we can
get out of this country

00:02:59.610 --> 00:03:01.113
is through them deporting us.

00:03:02.127 --> 00:03:06.010
- In Israel, I have so many cousins

00:03:06.010 --> 00:03:10.950
and so many aunts and uncles
and nieces and nephews

00:03:10.950 --> 00:03:14.210
and I feel like it's
come to the point where

00:03:14.210 --> 00:03:16.920
I don't know if I will ever meet them

00:03:16.920 --> 00:03:18.450
and I know a lot of my friends

00:03:18.450 --> 00:03:20.700
are best friends with their cousins.

00:03:20.700 --> 00:03:22.850
They get to go to Israel for vacation.

00:03:22.850 --> 00:03:25.310
I'm missing out on so much.

00:03:25.310 --> 00:03:27.680
- Personally, hearing all of these things

00:03:27.680 --> 00:03:29.590
that you guys are not able to enjoy

00:03:29.590 --> 00:03:32.863
about a country that I
live in is very difficult.

00:03:34.670 --> 00:03:38.660
What do you guys think
that you're missing out on?

00:03:38.660 --> 00:03:41.130
- The ability to simply go to school

00:03:41.130 --> 00:03:43.640
is the most important thing
to me, has been a struggle.

00:03:43.640 --> 00:03:45.700
We don't sleep at night.

00:03:45.700 --> 00:03:49.770
Just a million scenarios run
through my head every day.

00:03:49.770 --> 00:03:52.610
- I got robbed last week.

00:03:52.610 --> 00:03:54.010
I was scared to call the police

00:03:54.010 --> 00:03:57.080
because I didn't know
could they track my family?

00:03:57.080 --> 00:03:59.660
Would they get in touch with my parents?

00:03:59.660 --> 00:04:01.670
Would they come to my house?

00:04:01.670 --> 00:04:03.920
Would they wanna see who's there?

00:04:03.920 --> 00:04:05.433
Basically don't exist.

00:04:06.270 --> 00:04:08.190
- What is your biggest fear?

00:04:08.190 --> 00:04:10.940
- To have this adrenaline
every single day.

00:04:10.940 --> 00:04:13.940
To be scared every single
day for the rest of my life.

00:04:13.940 --> 00:04:16.190
That nothing will ever change.

00:04:16.190 --> 00:04:18.930
- My biggest fear is being detained

00:04:18.930 --> 00:04:21.660
and going through what my dad went though.

00:04:21.660 --> 00:04:24.670
I literally had a
nightmare last night about

00:04:24.670 --> 00:04:29.090
being dropped off in a country
that I've never been to

00:04:29.090 --> 00:04:30.410
since I was three.

00:04:30.410 --> 00:04:33.300
That I wouldn't even know
where I was standing.

00:04:33.300 --> 00:04:35.660
- With all of this fear that you guys

00:04:35.660 --> 00:04:37.430
have to live with every day,

00:04:37.430 --> 00:04:40.890
do you find that it's
really hard to trust people?

00:04:40.890 --> 00:04:42.440
- I've kept it a secret.

00:04:42.440 --> 00:04:43.790
I like to represent myself as Colombian

00:04:43.790 --> 00:04:44.660
because that's what I am,

00:04:44.660 --> 00:04:46.330
but people never really assume that

00:04:46.330 --> 00:04:48.680
I don't have a status in this country.

00:04:48.680 --> 00:04:51.620
When we received new that our
private bill was taken away

00:04:51.620 --> 00:04:53.560
and we were left without status,

00:04:53.560 --> 00:04:55.530
my biggest fear at the
time was I was gonna leave

00:04:55.530 --> 00:04:58.190
without anyone knowing
what happened to me.

00:04:58.190 --> 00:05:02.850
So I made a crazy decision
to tell my friend Brian.

00:05:02.850 --> 00:05:05.130
He was someone that was very open to it

00:05:05.130 --> 00:05:09.200
and made me feel very
comfortable talking to someone

00:05:09.200 --> 00:05:10.930
and if it wasn't for that conversation,

00:05:10.930 --> 00:05:13.383
I don't think I would've ever
spoken to someone about it.

00:05:15.520 --> 00:05:17.520
It makes me cry just because
of how special that moment was

00:05:17.520 --> 00:05:19.420
and we got really close because of it,

00:05:19.420 --> 00:05:21.910
but it was definitely hard at the time.

00:05:21.910 --> 00:05:24.690
I want people to know about my situation.

00:05:24.690 --> 00:05:26.580
I need people to know about my situation.

00:05:26.580 --> 00:05:28.267
And yeah, Selena.

00:05:28.267 --> 00:05:29.653
And yeah, Selena.

00:05:32.420 --> 00:05:33.521
You're good, thank you.

00:05:33.521 --> 00:05:35.310
- You really got me going here.

00:05:35.310 --> 00:05:37.490
When it came to high school,

00:05:37.490 --> 00:05:38.950
it would bring up a lot of questions.

00:05:38.950 --> 00:05:41.040
Everyone would always ask why
don't you have your license?

00:05:41.040 --> 00:05:41.900
Why don't you have a car?

00:05:41.900 --> 00:05:43.690
Why do you keep moving houses?

00:05:43.690 --> 00:05:47.190
If a question came up
between a close friend and I,

00:05:47.190 --> 00:05:48.360
I wouldn't hide it from them

00:05:48.360 --> 00:05:52.470
because I feel like it is
hard to find people you trust

00:05:52.470 --> 00:05:54.670
but it depends on how
long you've known them

00:05:54.670 --> 00:05:56.600
or what their situation is,

00:05:56.600 --> 00:05:58.730
what their beliefs are.

00:05:58.730 --> 00:06:01.323
- Do you feel American?

00:06:02.160 --> 00:06:04.150
How would you describe that feeling?

00:06:04.150 --> 00:06:06.520
- I feel like you couldn't
get any more American

00:06:06.520 --> 00:06:08.850
than us four at this table right now.

00:06:08.850 --> 00:06:10.230
- I feel like I am an American.

00:06:10.230 --> 00:06:11.450
I've lived here my whole life.

00:06:11.450 --> 00:06:13.150
I was six months old when I moved.

00:06:13.150 --> 00:06:15.500
I don't know anything but here.

00:06:15.500 --> 00:06:17.770
I don't want anyone to have to fear

00:06:17.770 --> 00:06:19.453
the place that they grew up in.

00:06:20.870 --> 00:06:22.370
I don't want anyone to experience that

00:06:22.370 --> 00:06:25.530
and I just want America as a whole to know

00:06:25.530 --> 00:06:27.670
and understand what's really happening

00:06:27.670 --> 00:06:29.560
when these people are getting deported.

00:06:29.560 --> 00:06:30.920
They don't just get a plane ticket

00:06:30.920 --> 00:06:34.690
and say, "Bye, go back to your old life."

00:06:34.690 --> 00:06:37.030
We don't have an old life anymore.

00:06:37.030 --> 00:06:38.193
This is what we have.

00:06:39.397 --> 00:06:41.640
- I don't know what else
I would be considered.

00:06:41.640 --> 00:06:44.530
I have Colombian family
who would tease me.

00:06:44.530 --> 00:06:45.590
They see me as American.

00:06:45.590 --> 00:06:46.650
I speak English.

00:06:46.650 --> 00:06:48.970
My Spanish isn't the strongest.

00:06:48.970 --> 00:06:51.360
I've lived here since I was three.

00:06:51.360 --> 00:06:52.900
It's my whole life.

00:06:52.900 --> 00:06:55.470
- What you see on the news is
not really what's happening.

00:06:55.470 --> 00:06:57.510
They're trying to label me as a criminal.

00:06:57.510 --> 00:07:00.030
They're trying to label
people as much as possible.

00:07:00.030 --> 00:07:02.090
We're not a threat to society.

00:07:02.090 --> 00:07:04.400
We're simply just being
looked at differently

00:07:04.400 --> 00:07:07.780
and portrayed as an enemy.

00:07:07.780 --> 00:07:09.690
- There's millions of us here

00:07:09.690 --> 00:07:13.540
and you don't hear about
I would say 99% of them

00:07:13.540 --> 00:07:15.660
simply because these are
people who just come here

00:07:15.660 --> 00:07:17.359
looking for a better life

00:07:17.359 --> 00:07:19.830
and they're working and they're
minding their own business.

00:07:19.830 --> 00:07:21.860
- I feel like we've been
given the stereotype

00:07:21.860 --> 00:07:24.250
that immigrants have
come here to sell drugs,

00:07:24.250 --> 00:07:29.090
to rob, to hurt, to steal, to
do all these terrible things

00:07:29.090 --> 00:07:33.060
when in reality we've come
here to live a safer life

00:07:33.060 --> 00:07:34.990
and instead of looking at us as people

00:07:34.990 --> 00:07:36.430
who wanna take from you,

00:07:36.430 --> 00:07:39.680
look at us as people
who want to be with you.

00:07:39.680 --> 00:07:41.690
We wanna be able to work together.

00:07:41.690 --> 00:07:45.030
- I really hope that the fight
doesn't end with us leaving.

00:07:45.030 --> 00:07:47.610
I hope that the fight
continues to the point where

00:07:47.610 --> 00:07:51.430
this country welcomes us with open arms

00:07:51.430 --> 00:07:54.290
and sees us for who we really are.

00:07:54.290 --> 00:07:56.360
We really just wanna make
sure this story's known

00:07:56.360 --> 00:07:57.760
and at the end of the day

00:07:57.760 --> 00:07:59.000
that's all that really matters to me

00:07:59.000 --> 00:08:01.993
is that this doesn't
happen to other families.

00:08:03.799 --> 00:08:06.249
- I hope for my family to
one day live in a place

00:08:07.672 --> 00:08:08.940
- I hope for my family to
one day live in a place

00:08:08.940 --> 00:08:10.870
where we're completely accepted

00:08:10.870 --> 00:08:14.780
and we don't feel constant fear

00:08:14.780 --> 00:08:17.850
and I hope that this
country comes to realize

00:08:17.850 --> 00:08:21.470
the complete injustice that's being done

00:08:21.470 --> 00:08:25.150
and that one day we can live in an America

00:08:25.150 --> 00:08:27.010
that is open to immigrants

00:08:27.010 --> 00:08:31.320
and lives up to its values
of freedom and liberty.

00:08:31.320 --> 00:08:32.580
- You guys have given me hope.

00:08:32.580 --> 00:08:34.900
There are beautiful
people in this world that

00:08:34.900 --> 00:08:38.010
do want this country to
change and to improve

00:08:38.010 --> 00:08:41.430
and seek logic in the situation.

00:08:41.430 --> 00:08:46.430
- What do you hope for the
future of America for us?

00:08:46.444 --> 00:08:48.940
(Bar laughs)
(Selena laughs)

00:08:48.940 --> 00:08:52.430
- Well, a huge part of why I
wanted to be a part of this

00:08:52.430 --> 00:08:57.000
is to also be a voice for
so many people who can't

00:08:57.000 --> 00:08:59.640
and are terrified to speak about it.

00:08:59.640 --> 00:09:04.640
I don't even think people
realize that my family

00:09:04.660 --> 00:09:06.100
also has a background.

00:09:06.100 --> 00:09:08.383
My grandparents were immigrants.

00:09:10.310 --> 00:09:13.670
To just think about the
life that I've been given

00:09:13.670 --> 00:09:14.833
and how blessed I am.

00:09:17.550 --> 00:09:19.613
My hope is that I see change.

00:09:21.200 --> 00:09:22.650
- We're all in this together.

00:09:24.570 --> 00:09:25.520
- Doesn't end here.

00:09:27.470 --> 00:09:29.233
- I think you are wonderful people.

00:09:32.790 --> 00:09:34.260
And I want you to stay.

